# 에필로그 새 문장 번역 1: 묘사(일 · 달 · 해) + 화면 문구. 열쇠 = 검수 페이지의 줄 번호, 값 = (영어, 일본어). {N} = 서번트 이름
TR = {
'n_day.0': ("The city greeted the morning as if nothing had happened. A construction notice went up in front of the collapsed wall.", "街は何事もなかったかのように朝を迎えた。崩れた塀の前に工事の案内板が立った。"),
'n_day.1': ("{N} stood at the traffic light for a long time. Only after the green had come and gone twice did they cross.", "{N}は信号の前でしばらく立ち尽くしていた。青が二度過ぎてから、ようやく渡った。"),
'n_day.1@now': ("At the traffic light, {N} scanned the rooftops out of habit. Realizing what they had been counting, they gave a wry smile.", "{N}は信号の前で、癖のように屋上を見回した。自分が何を数えていたのかに気づいて、苦笑した。"),
'n_day.2': ("The mark on the back of your hand was fainter than yesterday. {N} looked at it for a long while.", "手の甲の痕が昨日より薄くなった。{N}はそれを長いこと見つめていた。"),
'n_day.3': ("The news called that winter a gas accident. {N} watched to the end without changing the channel.", "ニュースはあの冬の出来事をガス事故と呼んだ。{N}はチャンネルを変えず、最後まで見ていた。"),
'n_day.4': ("You hung out the laundry. {N} was gripping a hanger like a weapon, and you laughed once.", "洗濯物を干した。{N}がハンガーを武器のように握っていたので、一度笑った。"),
'n_day.5': ("It rained. {N} sat by the window listening. They said it was the first rain with nothing to fight.", "雨が降った。{N}は窓辺に座って雨音を聞いていた。戦うことのない雨は初めてだと言った。"),
'n_day.5@civil': ("It rained. {N} sat by the window listening. They said the rain of this age sounds the same.", "雨が降った。{N}は窓辺に座って雨音を聞いていた。この時代の雨も同じ音がすると言った。"),
'n_day.6': ("{N} came back from the convenience store. In the bag were seven of the same rice ball.", "{N}がコンビニから戻ってきた。袋の中には同じおにぎりが七つ入っていた。"),
'n_day.7': ("The night was quiet. You learned that getting used to quiet nights takes time, too.", "夜は静かだった。静かな夜に慣れるのにも時間がかかるのだと知った。"),
'n_day.7@civil': ("The night was quiet. {N} kept the light on and wrote something until late.", "夜は静かだった。{N}は灯りを消さず、遅くまで何かを書いていた。"),
'n_day.8': ("{N} set their shoes neatly in the entryway. Beside yours, half a hand's width apart.", "{N}が玄関に靴を揃えて置いた。あなたの靴の隣に、半歩ぶん離して。"),
'n_day.9': ("The shops reopened in the alley where the war had been. {N} read each sign aloud, one by one.", "戦いのあった路地に、また店が開いた。{N}は看板をひとつひとつ声に出して読んだ。"),
'n_day.9@now': ("The shops reopened in the alley where the war had been. {N} counted the ones that were gone and the ones that were new.", "戦いのあった路地に、また店が開いた。{N}はなくなった店と新しくできた店をひとつずつ数えた。"),
'n_day.10': ("{N} took a nap. As a Servant they never needed sleep, they said sheepishly on waking.", "{N}が昼寝をした。サーヴァントだった頃は眠る必要がなかったと、起きてから照れくさそうに言った。"),
'n_day.11': ("After dinner the two of you did the dishes. One bowl broke, and nobody died.", "夕食のあと、二人で皿を洗った。器がひとつ割れて、誰も死ななかった。"),
'n_day.12': ("In the morning you woke first to {N}'s presence. Not a guard's alertness — just the presence of a person.", "朝、{N}の気配で先に目が覚めた。警戒ではなく、ただの人の気配だった。"),
'n_day.13': ("It was the fourteenth night. You had spent exactly the length of that winter, this time without losing anyone.", "十四日目の夜だった。あの冬とちょうど同じ長さを、今度は誰も失わずに過ごした。"),
'n_day2.0': ("{N} wrote down the weather from the morning news. Knowing tomorrow's sky in advance still seemed a marvel to them.", "{N}が朝のニュースの天気を書き留めた。明日の空を先に知るということが、まだ不思議らしい。"),
'n_day2.0@now': ("{N} did the dishes with the morning news on. When the forecast came, they said the laundry should come in.", "{N}は朝のニュースをつけたまま皿を洗った。天気予報が流れると、洗濯物を取り込まなければと言った。"),
'n_day2.1': ("The mail carrier came by. {N} opened the mailbox three times, though nothing could be addressed to them.", "郵便配達が来た。{N}は郵便受けを三度開けた。自分宛てのものなど来るはずもないのに。"),
'n_day2.2': ("{N} went up and down the stairs counting the floors. They said they were learning the measure of this house with their body.", "{N}が階段を上り下りしながら階数を数えた。この家の寸法を体で覚えているところだと言った。"),
'n_day2.3': ("Lunch was leftovers. Eating what was left over was strange to {N}, and they soon came to like it.", "昼は残り物だった。{N}は残り物を食べるということに戸惑い、すぐに気に入った。"),
'n_day2.4': ("In the afternoon, sunlight reached deep into the living room. {N} sat in it, holding their palm open.", "午後、陽が居間の奥まで差し込んだ。{N}はその陽だまりに座り、掌を広げていた。"),
'n_day2.5': ("{N} went through your bookshelf from end to end. They wanted to know what you had read growing up.", "{N}があなたの本棚を端から端まで眺めた。何を読んで育った人なのか知りたいと言った。"),
'n_day2.6': ("Toward evening the neighborhood smelled of cooking. {N} opened the window and breathed it in for a long time.", "夕方、近所に飯を炊く匂いがした。{N}は窓を開けて、しばらく嗅いでいた。"),
'n_day2.7': ("The faucet was leaking. {N} spent an hour fixing it. Even afterward they turned it on several times to check.", "蛇口から水が漏れていた。{N}は一時間かけて直した。直したあとも何度かひねってみていた。"),
'n_day2.8': ("{N} was wearing mismatched socks. When you pointed it out, they looked down for a while and left them as they were.", "{N}が左右違う靴下を履いていた。教えると、しばらく見下ろしてから、そのままにした。"),
'n_day2.9': ("A siren sounded somewhere in the city. {N}'s shoulders stiffened, then eased when they learned it was an ambulance.", "街のどこかでサイレンが鳴った。{N}の肩が強張り、救急車だと知って緩んだ。"),
'n_day2.9@now': ("A siren sounded somewhere in the city. {N}'s feet turned toward the door first, then stopped. It was no longer their job.", "街のどこかでサイレンが鳴った。{N}の足が先に玄関へ向かい、止まった。もう自分の仕事ではなかった。"),
'n_day2.10': ("{N} quietly watched you work. They said they liked seeing you when you weren't fighting.", "{N}はあなたが働く姿を静かに見ていた。戦っていないあなたを見るのが好きだと言った。"),
'n_day2.11': ("Brushing your teeth at night, your eyes met in the mirror. You both laughed with mouths full of foam.", "夜、歯を磨きながら鏡の中で目が合った。二人とも泡をくわえたまま笑った。"),
'n_day2.12': ("{N} learned to fold bedding. The next morning even yours had been folded.", "{N}が布団の畳み方を覚えた。翌朝、あなたの布団まで畳まれていた。"),
'n_day2.13': ("Children passed outside the window. {N} stayed there until their laughter faded.", "窓の外を子どもたちが通り過ぎた。{N}はその笑い声が遠ざかるまで窓辺にいた。"),
'n_day2.14': ("{N} overslept for the first time. Once up, they acted as though they had done something terribly wrong.", "{N}が初めて寝坊をした。起きてからは、大きな過ちを犯した人のように振る舞った。"),
'n_day2.15': ("The two of you drank tea in silence. Only the clink of cups. It was comfortable.", "二人で黙ってお茶を飲んだ。茶器の触れる音だけがした。心地よかった。"),
'n_day2.16': ("{N} began crossing off days on the calendar. Not days survived, they said — just days gone by.", "{N}が暦に印をつけ始めた。生き延びた日ではなく、ただ過ぎた日を数えているのだと言った。"),
'n_day2.17': ("On the way home in the evening with the shopping, {N} wordlessly took the heavier bag.", "夕方、買い物袋を提げて帰る道で、{N}は黙って重い方を持っていった。"),
'n_day2.18': ("{N} noticed one of your habits: rubbing the back of your hand when you think. A habit from that winter.", "{N}があなたの癖にひとつ気づいた。考えるときに手の甲をさすること。あの冬についた癖だ。"),
'n_day2.19': ("There were now two umbrellas in the stand by the door.", "玄関の傘立てに、傘が二本になった。"),
'n_day2.20': ("{N} ran a finger along the dust on the windowsill. They learned that dust gathers in a house where people live.", "{N}が窓枠の埃を指でなぞった。人の住む家には埃が積もるのだと知った。"),
'n_day2.20@now': ("{N} ran a finger along the dust on the windowsill and, without a word, fetched a cloth.", "{N}が窓枠の埃を指でなぞり、黙って雑巾を取ってきた。"),
'n_day2.21': ("Before turning off the light, {N} asked what tomorrow held. The answer was “nothing much.” {N} liked that answer.", "灯りを消す前に、{N}が明日の予定を尋ねた。答えは「別に何も」だった。{N}はその答えが好きだった。"),
'n_day2.22': ("{N} studied the magnets on the refrigerator one by one. They were the places you had been.", "{N}が冷蔵庫の磁石をひとつひとつ眺めた。あなたが訪れた場所だった。"),
'n_day2.23': ("You walked a lap around the neighborhood. {N} memorized every alley's name — not as escape routes, but as walking paths.", "近所を一回りした。{N}は路地の名前をすべて覚えた。退路としてではなく、散歩道として。"),
'n_day2.24': ("{N} nodded off at the table. You fetched a blanket without waking them.", "{N}が食卓でうとうとしていた。起こさずに毛布を持ってきた。"),
'n_day2.25': ("Today truly nothing happened. When you said so in the evening, {N} laughed.", "今日は本当に何もなかった。夕方そう言うと、{N}が笑った。"),
'n_day2.26': ("{N} called your name. There was no reason. They just wanted to say it.", "{N}があなたの名前を呼んだ。用はなかった。ただ呼んでみたかったと言った。"),
'n_day2.27': ("Before sleep, through the door, {N} said good night. Hearing it had already become a habit.", "眠る前、扉の向こうから{N}がおやすみと言った。それを聞くのが、もう習慣になっていた。"),
'n_mon.2': ("The cherry blossoms bloomed and fell. {N} watched the speed of the falling petals for a long time.", "桜が咲いて散った。{N}は花びらの落ちる速さをしばらく見ていた。"),
'n_mon.3': ("The days grew longer. Short sleeves appeared in {N}'s closet.", "日が長くなった。{N}の箪笥に半袖が増えた。"),
'n_mon.4': ("The rainy season began. Two umbrellas hung side by side in the entryway.", "梅雨が始まった。玄関に傘が二本、並んで掛かった。"),
'n_mon.5': ("The cicadas cried. {N} rarely left the front of the fan.", "蝉が鳴いた。{N}は扇風機の前をなかなか離れなかった。"),
'n_mon.6': ("At summer's end, fireworks sounded far away. {N} flinched once, then laughed.", "夏の終わり、遠くで花火の音がした。{N}は一度びくりとして、笑った。"),
'n_mon.7': ("The wind turned cool. On the way to the market, {N} picked up the shopping basket first.", "風が涼しくなった。買い物に行く道で、{N}が先に買い物かごを持った。"),
'n_mon.8': ("The ginkgo leaves fell. {N} had come to know these streets better than you.", "銀杏の葉が落ちた。{N}はこの町の道を、あなたよりよく知るようになった。"),
'n_mon.9': ("The first frost came. Together you took out the winter bedding.", "初霜が降りた。二人で冬の布団を出した。"),
'n_mon.10': ("Winter came again. The back of your hand felt a little cold, and that was all.", "また冬が来た。手の甲が少し冷えたが、それだけだった。"),
'n_mon.11': ("A year since that winter drew near. {N} had drawn a small circle on that date on the calendar.", "あの冬から一年が近づいた。暦のその日に、{N}が小さな丸をつけていた。"),
'n_mon.12': ("A year had passed. The snow melted, and the mark on your hand now showed only in sunlight.", "一年が過ぎた。雪が解け、手の甲の痕は今や陽の下でしか見えなかった。"),
'n_mon2.2.0': ("Spring rain fell for days. {N} came to like the smell of earth after the rain.", "春の雨が何日か降った。{N}は雨上がりの土の匂いが好きになった。"),
'n_mon2.2.1': ("Children of the new school term passed through the neighborhood. {N} worried their bags were too big.", "近所を新学期の子どもたちが行き来した。{N}はあの鞄は大きすぎると心配した。"),
'n_mon2.3.0': ("The wind grew gentle. {N} slept with the window open for the first time.", "風が柔らかくなった。{N}は初めて窓を開けたまま眠った。"),
'n_mon2.3.1': ("Fresh green came in. {N} noticed the same road changing a little every day.", "新緑が萌えた。{N}は同じ道が日ごとに少しずつ変わっていくのに気づいた。"),
'n_mon2.4.0': ("Days went by when the laundry would not dry. {N} bought something called a dehumidifier.", "洗濯物の乾かない日が続いた。{N}が除湿剤というものを買ってきた。"),
'n_mon2.4.1': ("The hydrangeas bloomed. Told they change color, {N} watched them for days.", "紫陽花が咲いた。色の変わる花だと聞いて、{N}は何日も見守った。"),
'n_mon2.5.0': ("It was hot even at night. You walked together to the convenience store for ice cream.", "夜も暑かった。二人でコンビニまで歩いてアイスを食べた。"),
'n_mon2.5.1': ("A shower passed. {N} learned how to wait out the rain under the eaves.", "夕立が過ぎた。{N}は軒下で雨宿りすることを覚えた。"),
'n_mon2.6.0': ("You split a watermelon. {N} learned from the children how to spit the seeds far.", "西瓜を二つに割った。{N}は種を遠くへ飛ばすやり方を子どもたちに教わってきた。"),
'n_mon2.6.1': ("It was a sweltering night. {N} gave up on sleep and counted stars from the balcony.", "熱帯夜だった。{N}は眠るのを諦めて、ベランダで星を数えた。"),
'n_mon2.7.0': ("Long sleeves in the mornings and evenings. {N}'s closet had grown by a season.", "朝夕は長袖を着た。{N}の箪笥が一季節ぶん増えた。"),
'n_mon2.7.1': ("The sky grew high. {N} said this was the season they liked best.", "空が高くなった。{N}はこの季節がいちばん気に入ったと言った。"),
'n_mon2.8.0': ("You swept the fallen leaves. They piled up again the next day. {N} did not mind the wasted effort.", "落ち葉を掃いた。掃いても次の日にはまた積もった。{N}はその無駄骨を嫌がらなかった。"),
'n_mon2.8.1': ("The smell of roasted sweet potatoes drifted through the alley. {N} burned their fingers peeling one.", "焼き芋の匂いが路地に漂った。{N}は指を焦がしながら皮を剥いた。"),
'n_mon2.9.0': ("Your breath showed white. {N} blew out the white from their own mouth again and again.", "息が白くなった。{N}は自分の口から出る白いものを何度も吹いてみた。"),
'n_mon2.9.1': ("You brought out the heater. {N} would not leave it, and their back roasted red.", "ストーブを出した。{N}がその前を離れないので、背中が赤く焼けた。"),
'n_mon2.10.0': ("The first snow fell. {N} opened the window and held a hand out for a long time.", "初雪が降った。{N}は窓を開けて、長いこと手を差し出していた。"),
'n_mon2.10.1': ("Lights were strung along the streets. {N} said there had been no time to look at them that winter.", "通りに灯りの飾りが掛かった。{N}は、あの冬にはこれを見る暇がなかったと言った。"),
'n_mon2.11.0': ("It was the time of the longest nights. A night as long as that winter's was, this year, quiet.", "夜のいちばん長い頃だった。あの冬と同じ長さの夜が、今年は静かだった。"),
'n_mon2.11.1': ("You bought a box of mandarins. {N}'s fingertips were stained yellow.", "蜜柑を一箱買った。{N}の指先が黄色く染まった。"),
'n_mon2.12.0': ("The snow began to melt. About this time a year ago, red first showed on the back of your hand.", "雪が解け始めた。一年前の今頃、手の甲に初めて赤いものが浮かんだ。"),
'n_mon2.12.1': ("Spring was coming. Your second spring with {N}.", "春が近づいていた。{N}と迎える二度目の春だ。"),
'n_yr.0': ("One more spring with {N} went by.", "{N}と迎える春が、またひとつ過ぎた。"),
'n_yr.1': ("Little by little, the things in the house became the two of yours.", "家の中の物が、少しずつ二人のものになっていった。"),
'n_yr.2': ("{N} now changed trains without looking at the route map.", "{N}はもう路線図を見ずに乗り換えた。"),
'n_yr.2@now': ("{N} now knew the neighborhood shortcuts better than you.", "{N}はもう近所の近道を、あなたよりよく知っていた。"),
'n_yr.3': ("The neighbors called {N} by name. The name used in this world.", "近所の人たちは{N}を名前で呼んだ。この世界で使う名前で。"),
'n_yr.4': ("The days you spoke of that winter dwindled to once or twice a year.", "あの冬の話をする日は、年に一度か二度に減った。"),
'n_yr.5': ("The shoes in the entryway changed a few times. Where they were set stayed the same.", "玄関の靴は何度か替わった。置かれる場所はそのままだった。"),
'n_yr.6': ("{N} came to speak of their former life like a joke.", "{N}は生前のことを冗談のように話すようになった。"),
'n_yr.7': ("A photo album filled up.", "アルバムが一冊埋まった。"),
'n_yr.8': ("It was an ordinary year. You both knew how rare that was.", "平凡な年だった。それがどれほど稀なことか、二人とも知っていた。"),
'n_yr2.0': ("{N} became one of the longest-standing residents of the neighborhood.", "{N}はこの町でいちばん長く住んでいる部類になった。"),
'n_yr2.1': ("One familiar shop closed, and one new shop opened.", "行きつけの店がひとつ閉まり、新しい店がひとつ開いた。"),
'n_yr2.2': ("{N}'s papers were renewed once. The face in the photo had changed a little.", "{N}の書類が一度更新された。写真の顔が少し変わっていた。"),
'n_yr2.3': ("Heavy rain in summer, little snow in winter. That was about the biggest news of the year.", "夏に大雨が降り、冬は雪が少なかった。今年の大事はそのくらいだった。"),
'n_yr2.4': ("{N} had what is called a health checkup. They stuck the results on the refrigerator.", "{N}が健康診断というものを受けた。結果の紙を冷蔵庫に貼った。"),
'n_yr2.5': ("One piece of furniture was replaced. Choosing it took three months.", "家具がひとつ替わった。選ぶのに三か月かかった。"),
'n_yr2.6': ("{N} used the old speech less. It came out now only when talking in their sleep.", "{N}が古い言葉を使うことは減った。たまに寝言でだけ出た。"),
'n_yr2.7': ("One more of your shared calendars came down from the wall.", "二人で使う暦が、また一冊壁から下りた。"),
'n_yr2.8': ("The neighborhood children greeted {N}. One more title had been added after the name.", "近所の子どもたちが{N}に挨拶した。名前のあとにつく呼び方がひとつ増えた。"),
'n_yr2.9': ("The nights you dreamed of that winter dwindled to about one a year.", "あの冬の夢を見る夜は、年に一度ほどに減った。"),
'n_yr2.10': ("{N}'s favorite season changed. This year it was autumn, they said.", "{N}の好きな季節が変わった。今年は秋だと言った。"),
'n_yr2.11': ("Your nagging came to resemble each other's.", "互いの小言が似てきた。"),
'n_yr2.12': ("New calluses formed on {N}'s hands. Calluses made by the work of this world.", "{N}の手に新しい胼胝ができた。この世界の仕事が作った胼胝だった。"),
'n_yr2.13': ("A newly moved-in neighbor asked whether you two had lived here long. You could answer that you had.", "越してきた隣人が尋ねた。お二人はここに長くお住まいですかと。そうだと答えることができた。"),
'n_yr2.14': ("{N} said “this time last year” for the first time. After that they said it often.", "{N}が初めて「去年の今頃」という言葉を使った。それからはよく使った。"),
'n_yr2.15': ("The films you had watched together passed a hundred. {N} had been counting.", "二人で観た映画が百本を超えた。{N}が数えていた。"),
'n_yr2.16': ("Every year the same flower bloomed in the same place. Going to check on it became a task.", "毎年同じ場所に同じ花が咲いた。それを確かめに行くのが仕事になった。"),
'n_yr2.17': ("You started to write that it was an uneventful year, then realized that was the biggest event of all.", "何事もない年だったと書こうとして、それがいちばんの大事なのだと気づいた。"),
}
